 "notes": "Complex at ul. Pyskowicka 39, Tarnowskie Góry (Silesia): 16th-century castle, 36 hotel rooms, restaurant, conference pavilion, AVATAR medical clinic. Building area 10,683.7 m², site 35,896 m² (teaser). Owners Rajner and Katarzyna Smolorz, 1/2 each.\nStructure (memory): mortgage on the conference pavilion GL1T/00088570/5 + pledge on the collection; clinic excluded. Repayment from selling both. Memo break-even: pavilion must sell for at least PLN 3.5m if the collection sells for PLN 2.0m.\nASSUMPTIONS: loan PLN 4.30m sized so the break-even sales (net of 5% selling costs) just repay loan + rolled-up interest + catch-up; terms as the Ustroń precedent (11.5% + 1.5% catch-up, 8% fee withheld, 24 m bullet); interest rolled up because no hotel P&L is in the model; drawdown 1 Dec 2026; collection sold month 13, pavilion month 21; 100% of net sale proceeds swept; purpose of funds unknown (entered as other uses).\nValuation gap: pavilion appraised at PLN 14.81m (Nov 2023, commissioned by Fundacja Kompleks Zamkowy Tarnowice Stare) vs PLN 3.5m realistic sale threshold – lending value set at the threshold (76% haircut). Castle complex PLN 32.407m (16 Oct 2026, of which clinic ≈ PLN 12.19m; Oct 2023 update PLN 21.914m) is shown for reference only, not pledged.\nKey issues (memory): no registered public road access (easement needed, KC art. 145 / KPC art. 1000); castle, restaurant and clinic in one land register; clinic built with EU subsidies (durability / clawback); compulsory mortgage PLN 200,206.58 on the castle register.",
